      ⍝ Bugs28 #57 regression (Bugs27 #56 residual): dyadic ¨ (like
      ⍝ ∘.f, f⍤y, and f.g) still broke when the operand changed ⎕IO --
      ⍝ Z__vA_LO_EACH_vB/sB and Z__sA_LO_EACH_vB (Macro.def) indexed
      ⍝ μ1/μ2/μ6 with the raw loop counter μ8, seeded from ⎕IO ONCE at
      ⍝ the start; if LO's own ⎕IO←0 (global, not auto-localized in a
      ⍝ lambda) persisted past its first call, every later iteration's
      ⍝ indexing (relative to the NEW ⎕IO) silently misaligned instead
      ⍝ of INDEX-ERROR-ing outright, unlike the ALREADY-fixed monadic ¨
      ⍝ (Z__LO_EACH_B). Fixed the same self-correcting way: recompute
      ⍝ ⎕IO+(μ8-savedIO) fresh at each use instead of trusting μ8 alone.
      ⍝ 1+⍳2 (⎕IO=0) = 1 2; 2+⍳3 (⎕IO now 0 from the first call, but
      ⍝ self-correctingly still right) = 2 3 4.
      ⍝
      1 2 {⎕IO←0 ⋄ ⍺+⍳⍵}¨ 2 3
 1 2  2 3 4 

      ⎕IO←1

